 1. The spawn prompt opens with the `brief header` (§5.3) and the line "Read your brief at <path>."; PreToolUse on `Agent` carries `tool_input.prompt`, `description`, `subagent_type`, `model` (r1-team-facts addendum; `name` and `team_name` are read by CDP5, `guard-spawn.mjs:13-14`, and confirmed by probe A-1).
-2. `guard-spawn.mjs` denies: in an active run any `subagent_type` not of the form `cdp6-core:<role>` (TM-6; a bare `cdp6-core:` names no role and is denied too); a named spawn outside a phase whose card allows team mode or without a team gate (§3.4 item 1); a missing or malformed header; a brief failing `brief-lint.mjs`; a base diff on cited paths (O7); a third worker spawn or third review round per task (O14); two concurrent spawns of the same role for the same task; from SL-2c, a spawn of a capture-bound role (in stage 1 `cdp6-core:devils-advocate`; from SL-3 every role whose capture a gate counts; the set is defined once, `captureBound` of `lib/agent-name.mjs`, which `lib/verdict-index.mjs` imports, `review-code` run 85 🟢-3: the SL-2c build defines it twice, `lib/agent-name.mjs:10`, `lib/verdict-index.mjs:89`) while a bound spawn of the same role (bound to an `agent_id` at `SubagentStart`, step 3) is neither closed by its capture nor `void`, whatever its task, unless a fan-out or team record (SL-3, SL-11) admits it (retro 0021-S1 RC-E: live P1 run 1 spawned D-2 while the D-1 spawn was pending and bound, against the owner's "one after the other", ledger 0021, 2026-11-05T10:37:24+01:00, record `live-p1-run-1.md:12`; AC-12.35); until SL-3 an unbound pending spawn of the role does not block such a spawn, because no stage-1 hook marks a spawn that never launched `void` (another hook denied the `Agent` call, or the prompt was declined; the resolver of AC-12.20 comes with SL-3), so counting it blocked every later spawn of the role (`adversarial-auditor` run 84 F5, `lib/counters.mjs:61-64` of the SL-2c build); the deny reason and preflight check (g) of UC-14 step 5 list the role's unbound pending spawns with the owner's way out, marking each `void` in `S/counters.json` by hand outside Claude Code; a retry admitted while such a spawn is still pending is not bound at its `SubagentStart`, because the binding of step 3 then finds two unbound pending spawns of the type and binds none (`lib/counters.mjs:76`, `hooks/inject-contract.mjs:44` of the SL-2c build), so its handback is refused as unbound (`hooks/check-handback.mjs:91`) and the owner's way out comes first (Q-25); two capture-bound spawns in one message stay a stage-1 residual as well, since the second one's PreToolUse comes before the first one's `SubagentStart` (A-18; Q-25); a spawn of a role while a pending spawn of the same role is still unbound (TM2-5; same-role workers of a wave are therefore spawned one after another); a concurrent spawn without a fan-out or team record (OR-1); any spawn by a caller with `agent_id` (workers spawn no subagents, C8c); a writer spawn whose `env:` names no worktree registered by `run.mjs worktree` (OR-9, UC-05 step 2). It records a pending spawn (task, role, `target:` hashes, time) in `counters.json`. A pending spawn is keyed by the `Agent` call's `tool_use_id`; it is marked `void` when, at the end of the caller's turn (`Stop`), that call has neither a PostToolUse nor a `SubagentStart` (another hook denied the `Agent` call, hooks.md:1965, or the prompt was declined: A-18 measured neither for a denied call, while an allowed call gets its PostToolUse at spawn time, record "Platform facts"); the caller's next PreToolUse no longer voids it, because with two spawns in one message the second spawn's PreToolUse comes before the first spawn's PostToolUse and `SubagentStart` (A-18, 2.1.314, record A-18 row and §11.4); `guard-spawn.mjs` is therefore also registered on PostToolUse with the matcher `Agent|Task` (records the launch) and on the main session's `Stop` (resolves the turn), both built in SL-3 with AC-12.20; until the turn ends an unresolved pending spawn still counts for the same-role rule of this step, so a same-role retry in the same turn after a declined prompt is denied with that reason and succeeds in the next turn (AC-12.20); a declined prompt may end the turn as a user interrupt, after which `Stop` does not run ("Does not run if the stoppage occurred due to a user interrupt", hooks.md:2726), so the caller's next `UserPromptSubmit` (hooks.md:1468) resolves the pending spawns of the ended turn the same way; when neither runs (both fail open, and whether `Stop` fires after an interrupted turn is not measured, §11.4), the pending spawn stays pending, which blocks its role (fail closed), and the phase-exit reconciliation (OR-37), which `run.mjs exit` runs before it checks the gate verdicts, voids it on model-unwritable evidence, an `Agent` PreToolUse line with no PostToolUse and no `SubagentStart` in the hook log; a pending spawn with a PostToolUse stays open until its `SubagentStart` binds it and its handback closes it, and one still without `SubagentStart` at the caller's `Stop` is a reconciliation gap of OR-37, cleared only as OR-37 says; a void spawn counts as no spawn, no round and no reconciliation gap (r3-KR N8).
